Done. Here's what I shipped:

`/skill install <path>` — the first step toward a skills marketplace. It copies a local skill directory into ~/.config/yoyo/skills/<name>/ so users can permanently install skills they find or create.

Implementation details:
• extract_skill_name_from_frontmatter() — parses YAML frontmatter for the name: field, handles quoted/unquoted values
• `skill_install()` — full validation pipeline: checks path exists → is a directory → contains SKILL.md → has valid frontmatter with name → not already installed → copies recursively
• copy_dir_recursive() — walks the source tree and copies all files/subdirs
• skill_install_to() — test-only variant with configurable destination directory
• Rolls back partial installs on copy failure
• Uses the same XDG config pattern as the rest of yoyo (XDG_CONFIG_HOME → ~/.config)

14 new tests covering:
• Frontmatter parsing (valid, quoted, single-quoted, no frontmatter, no name, empty name)
• Install errors (nonexistent path, not a directory, missing SKILL.md, bad frontmatter, already exists)
• Successful install with file verification
• Subdirectory copying
• Subcommand routing

